WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
what should we do  begin the next game  squid game may have reached global  success but along the way they made some  changes some that went well and others  that have only garnered more criticism  when did you realize  the show became so big right now  when squid game came out and its  popularity began to rise one would think  that the hard work was over but that  wasn't the case with the netflix hit the  show faced serious backlash because the  numbers used on the squid game business  cards were real and belonged to some  residents in south korea if those people  didn't know what squid game was before  they definitely knew when their phones  were blowing up with messages and phone  calls from fans of the kdrama a dessert  shop owner in south korea saw the  effects squid game had on fans pretty  directly her business number was one of  the few shown on screen in the show she  started getting endless phone calls 24  hours a day it's not all jokes though  some of the callers were actually asking  to be part of the game or just to  express their anger and yell  the shop owner had over 4 000 different  numbers trying to reach her clogging up  her business line and affecting her  sugar-free sweet bean jelly's sales  another number belonged to a man who  received so many calls and messages that  his phone was regularly dying throughout  the day not only that he couldn't even  get any of the calls or messages that  were actually meant for him while  netflix worked quickly to edit and cut  scenes where the real phone numbers  appeared for some reason they do still  make the screen for australian viewers  once the show had finished filming the  time came for it to be dubbed over in  different languages one of the actors  who performed the english dubbing was a  big fan of the fact that all his cast  mates were either of korean or asian  heritage which turned out to be a huge  plus when they were recording in the  studio as they came across some  inconsistencies and mistranslations  throughout the script they took a moment  to bring it to the production crew and  change the already written script the  cast did a great job at bringing clarity  to the scenes korean actors even if not  fluent can call out something if it's  not right is how edward hong who did the  dubbing for the priest character put it  he had a better understanding of  specifically how certain people would  speak like the religious character he  portrayed meaning he was able to tell if  something didn't quite click dubbing is  a very specific skill on its own since  the actors need to vocally match the  on-screen performance and visuals so to  be able to change dialogue on the go is  really raising the bar  it's our time to face the lord  while loads of people around the globe  love squid game not everyone is a fan of  what turned out to be some pretty  misleading subtitles when it came to the  english version on netflix translating a  show from its original language is a  tricky job and unfortunately in the case  of squid game many of the subtleties and  meanings were lost in translation which  does do quite a disservice to the  original writer who put together such a  tight script not only that the english  dubbing and the english subtitles also  have variations between them making it a  pretty strange watching experience  i'm better than you think and i'm  stronger than most guys too number two  on two's character was majorly impacted  by this the english translation we get  is  i'm not a genius but i still got it  where it goes when in reality she's  saying i'm very smart i just never got a  chance to study the meanings are pretty  different and the actual line also works  as a reference to a trope of characters  with smarts but not a whole lot of money  that's regularly seen in korean  television  these changes from the original script  didn't work out so well  i'll do anything you tell me i'm not a  regular girl  episode 1 of squid game is called red  light green light but in korean it's a  very different story the original title  of the episode translates to the day  that the mugunga flower blossomed a play  on the name of the game in korea it's a  long but beautiful title and it  definitely isn't even close to the  english one we got what makes this  really frustrating is that we lose a lot  of cultural significance since the  mungungua flower symbolizes beginnings  and is the national flower of korea  depending on who you're talking to or  where you are squid game can also be  referred to as round six it's even the  official title of the show on imdb round  six was the name the show was called  when netflix announced the production in  2019 but when it was time to launch the  show they went with the title we've all  come to hear so often  what we see on screen in the subtitles  and what we hear are two very different  things when it comes to the english  translations if watching the show in  korean the english subtitles don't  feature a small but significant line in  which player 1 says there is no  ownership between me and you the fact  that the subtitles were changed not to  include it deeply affects how we  interpret this  definitely not a great change  on the road to worldwide success  netflix's squid game definitely hits  some speed bumps with the data leaking  and misleading translations but it  hasn't held back the team at all in fact  one change made on the go brought one of  the greatest small moments in the show  guillen picking up sebioc's coffee cup  was total improv  considering it took 10 years for the  show to actually get made it seems like  all the time money and effort was  definitely worth it  what would you do if your number was the  one featured on squid game

